# Architecture Pressure Docs

Use `enclosure architecture pressure` to inspect callable fan-out, callable fan-in, wide signatures, and public API export pressure.

## When To Use It

- Before refactoring an orchestration-heavy module.
- When looking for prop drilling or repeated parameter forwarding.
- When reviewing public seams and possible unnecessary re-exports.
- After a modwire upgrade that improves callable graph extraction.

## How To Respond

- Treat high fan-out callables as orchestration or algorithm-density review targets.
- Treat high fan-in callables as shared seam candidates.
- Treat wide signatures with call pressure as prop-drilling candidates.
- Treat re-export hubs as API review targets before broadening module seams.

